{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMjd23HgFx7t8FBFbfsd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #178 (user docs and a GitHub Pages site) as **done**: the engineer triage role plans it and the engineer worker implements it. The decision is written to `.ard/178/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **Why only the engineer:** it is the only triage role that exists. There is no product-manager, architect or documentation-planner role, so the engineer will choose the site generator and page structure alone.\n- **What the agent can do:** write the docs under `docs/`, add the site config, and add Go tests run by `make test` that check the documented commands and config keys against the code. It can also add the README link and update the proposal's Rollout section. None of that touches protected paths.\n- **Why not needs-human:** the Pages workflow and the CI steps for the site build and link check live under `.github/`, which agents may not change. The issue itself already gives that work, and turning Pages on, to a human. So I routed it rather than holding it for a person.\n\nThe file's \"Open issues\" section tells maintainers:\n- They must add the `.github/` workflow and CI steps and enable Pages themselves.\n- They may want to review the engineer's plan before the worker starts, since it makes the design choices alone.\n- The work could be split into two PRs if one gets too big: docs content first, then the site and checks.\n- A person has to follow Getting started by hand on a scratch repo before the issue counts as done."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":857,"cache_read_input_tokens":12371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":857},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null